-$f(x)=x^2-2$ on the rational numbers in $[0,2]$: it is continuous, negative at $0$, positive at $2$, and never zero. What does $\R$ have that $\Q$ lacks? Find the exact step of the proof below that fails over $\Q$.
-\end{think}
